LOOP-RESTORATION EXTENT FIX — PRE/POST BYTE-IDENTITY A/B — 2026-08-06
=====================================================================
Issue:  imazen/zenav1-svt#11 (restoration.rs:985 index out of bounds)
Branch: fix/issue-11-lr-apply-true-dims (off main 4c5c13246)
Fix:    38b19bd4d
Host:   Darwin arm64 (aarch64), 2026-08-06
Tool:   an A/B driver over two builds of `svtav1/examples/identity_run`, one at
        main 4c5c13246 and one at the fix, comparing sha256 of the raw OBU
        stream per cell. Both binaries encode the SAME generated .yuv.
Summary (committed):  benchmarks/lr_align_extent_ab_2026-08-06.tsv
Full per-cell log (NOT committed, sha256 pairs):
        ~/tmp/zi11/ab_sweep.tsv

GRID — 19 dims x 5 presets {0,3,6,9,13} x 4 cli qps {1,20,40,63}
       x 2 bit depths {8,10} x 3 contents {uniform,gradient,screen} = 2,280 cells.
Dims chosen to cross every geometry class relative to the defect: 64-aligned
(64,128,256,512,320x256), 8-aligned-not-64 (56,72,120,200,384x512,766x384),
non-8-aligned that do NOT cross a count_units_in_tile(256,..) boundary
(65x64, 72x65, 257x120, 65x257, 258x258, 385x257, 500x504), and the one that
DOES (383x512 — the smallest rendition issue #11 reported).

RESULT
  SAME             2,266   byte-identical stream pre-fix and post-fix
  FIXED_UNPANICKED    14   pre-fix PANIC, post-fix a valid stream
  DIFF                 0   no cell that worked before changed its bytes

The 14 are all 383x512: gradient at p0/p3/p6 x qp{20,40,63} x bd{8,10} plus
screen at p6/q63 x bd{8,10} — i.e. exactly the cells where the frame-level
Wiener RD wins, which is what makes the defect content-dependent. 383 counts
one horizontal restoration unit ((383+128)/256 = 1) while the aligned 384
walks two, so a 1x2 grid received a 2x2 walk: "the len is 2 but the index is 2",
the message in the issue verbatim.

The other 18 dims are the control: no cell of theirs moved a byte, which is the
claim the fix rests on (an extent change that must be inert wherever true ==
aligned, and wherever the alignment does not cross a unit boundary).

CROSS-CHECKS AGAINST THE C ENCODER (same host, same day, all post-fix)
  tools/partial_sb_gate.sh          146/146 byte-identical
  tools/bd10_partial_sb_gate.sh     157/157 byte-identical (+5/5 pinned
                                    divergences still diverging, as pinned)
  tools/bd10_matrix.sh               36/36  byte-identical
  tools/regression_spotcheck.sh      26/26  (23 pre-existing + 3 new
                                    lr-align-cross-* cells)
  tools/arbitrary_size_robustness.sh 128/128 panic-free + aomdec-decodable
  Direct cells: `gradient 383x512 q40 p6` bd8 AND bd10, `gradient 766x128 q40 p6`,
  `gradient 258x128 q40 p6`, `gradient 385x257 q40 p6` — all IDENTICAL to the C
  encoder post-fix. The first three PANICKED pre-fix, so the port now matches C
  on input it previously could not encode at all.

WHY NO BITSTREAM CHANGE WAS POSSIBLE. `apply_restoration_frame` and
`save_lr_boundaries` run AFTER the tile has been entropy-coded; they touch only
the published recon. The defect could crash the encode or corrupt the recon, but
never the stream — which is why every non-panicking cell is byte-identical.

REPRODUCING THE FIVE REPORTED RENDITIONS. The real assets
(s3://zentrain/refs/imazen-26-hdr-grid-2026-06-14/) are not reachable from this
host and /mnt/v does not exist here, so the renditions were reproduced by
GEOMETRY with synthetic content at their exact dimensions — see
benchmarks/lr_align_extent_renditions_2026-08-06.tsv.

THE FIVE RENDITIONS BY GEOMETRY (lr_align_extent_renditions_2026-08-06.tsv)
Each reported rendition at its exact dims, bd10 4:2:0 preset 6, cli qp
{1,15,30,45,54,63} x {gradient,screen}: 60 cells, 42 SAME, 18 FIXED_UNPANICKED,
0 DIFF, 0 still broken. The observed panic indices match the arithmetic model
of the defect exactly:

  rendition    overflowing plane   grid (h x v)   walk (h x v)   observed panic
  383x512      luma                1 x 2          2 x 2          len 2, index 2
  2048x1660    luma                8 x 6          8 x 7          len 48, index 48
  1914x2560    luma                7 x 10         8 x 10         len 70, index 70
  766x1024     CHROMA              1 x 2          2 x 2          (not armed here)
  2297x3072    CHROMA              4 x 6          5 x 6          (not armed here)

The two CHROMA-side renditions stay SAME under this harness because
identity_run's synthetic content carries FLAT chroma (u = v = 128), so the
chroma planes pick RESTORE_NONE and the chroma unit walk never runs -- the same
reason the pre-existing synthetic robustness matrix could not reach this bug on
real photographs. The chroma half is covered instead by
`svtav1/tests/issue11_repro.rs::issue11_766x128_chroma_unit_walk_stays_in_the_grid`,
which feeds textured chroma at the identical crossing (true ceil(766/2) = 383 ->
1 unit, applied 768/2 = 384 -> 2) and panicked "len is 1 but the index is 1"
pre-fix.
